@meta
id: 18-02
title: Let Tab type the path
chapter: 18
type: lesson
skills: edit-file, wildmenu
par: 35
minutes: 4
vscode: Ctrl+P and a few letters
vimrc: set wildmenu wildmode=longest:full,full
open: README.md

@brief
The payment gateway has moved its refund endpoint. In the payment
service, the call to `/refunds` must become `/v2/refunds`. Nothing else
in that file changes.

The service lives under `src/infrastructure/services/`. Last lesson you
typed a path like that in full. This time, type one letter of each
directory and let Tab finish it. This lesson turns on `wildmenu` with
`wildmode=longest:full,full` for you; chapter 28 shows you how to keep
it.

Tab completes as much as is unambiguous. When only one entry matches, it
completes the whole thing and moves on. When several match, it fills in
the common prefix and shows the candidates in a bar along the bottom.

You may notice a couple of dot-files at the root that the dojo uses for
bookkeeping. Ignore them.

@keys
| `Tab` | complete the path on the command line |
| `Tab` again | cycle to the next candidate when several match |
| `Shift-Tab` | cycle back |
| `Ctrl-U` | clear the command line and start over |

@hints
`:e s` then Tab. Watch `src/` appear. Keep going: one letter, one Tab,
one directory deeper.
--
`s` Tab, `i` Tab, `s` Tab, `p` Tab. Four letters, four Tabs, one
Enter. Then search for `refunds`.
--
`:e s<Tab>i<Tab>s<Tab>p<Tab>` and Enter. `/refunds` lands on the word;
`iv2/` and `Esc` slot the prefix in. `:wq`.

@solution
    :e s<Tab>i<Tab>s<Tab>p<Tab><Enter>
    /refunds<Enter> iv2/ <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Twelve keystrokes for a forty-five character path. That is the whole
trick, and it works everywhere on the command line: `:w`, `:r`, `:sp`,
`:args`, `:cd`, `:set` values, `:help` topics.

`longest:full` is the setting that makes the first Tab conservative: it
only types what every candidate agrees on, then shows you the rest. The
second `full` means a further Tab walks through the candidates one at a
time. Without `wildmenu` you get the same completion but no bar, so you
cannot see what the choices were. Turn the bar on and leave it on.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Handles orders, customers and refunds for the storefront.

## Layout

    src/domain/<name>/<name>.entity.ts       the shape of a record
    src/domain/<name>/<name>.repository.ts   how it is loaded and saved
    src/domain/<name>/<name>.provider.ts     the business rules
    src/infrastructure/services/             calls to other systems
    src/configuration/errors/default.json    every error code we can throw

@start src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/refunds`, { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@expected src/infrastructure/services/payment.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';

@injectable()
export class PaymentService {
  public async refund(orderId: string) {
    const response = await this.http.post(`/v2/refunds`, { orderId });

    if (response.status !== 200) {
      throw exception('REFUND_FAILED');
    }

    return response.data;
  }
}

@start src/infrastructure/services/email.service.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';

@injectable()
export class EmailService {
  public async send(args: { to: string; template: string }) {
    return this.http.post(`/send`, args);
  }
}
